    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0297" n="285" xml:id="pg285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.01/5–545</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Council of People’s Commissars of
                        the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stalin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Truman </hi><anchor n="23" xml:id="d210-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>Since you are interested in the Polish question and should be familiar with Mr.
                    Churchill’s message to me concerning this question, dated April 28,<anchor
                        n="24" xml:id="d210-f2"/> I feel it appropriate to transmit to you the full
                    text of my reply to Mr. Churchill, sent to him on May 4, 1945.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-05"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >May</hi> 5, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d210-a1.xml" xpointer="d210-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d210-f1" n="23" type="source" xml:id="d210-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted on May 5, 1945, to the Acting Secretary of State by the Soviet
                    Chargé, Nikolay Vasilyevich Novikov.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d210-f2" n="24" xml:id="d210-f2-content">
                <p>See Prime Minister Churchill’s telegram 21, April 29, to President Truman, <ref
                        target="#pg265">p. 265</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
